## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates practical observability skills, including dashboard design, alerting configuration, and data quality enforcement in a real-world GCP pipeline. It also tests familiarity with synthetic testing methodologies to validate alerting behavior before production incidents occur.

## Key Concepts
- **Dataflow streaming pipeline**: Continuous ingestion from Pub/Sub to BigQuery with windowed processing
- **Custom Cloud Monitoring metrics**: Per-tenant granularity enables tenant-specific SLA tracking and anomaly detection
- **Dead-letter routing**: Data quality enforcement without data loss; invalid records are preserved for debugging
- **Synthetic testing**: Proactive validation of alerting thresholds under load conditions

## Code Example
```java
public class ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn extends DoFn<String, TableRow> {
  private final Counter validRecords;
  private final Counter invalidRecords;
  private final Distribution latencyDistribution;

  public ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn(String tenantId) {
    this.validRecords = Metrics.counter(ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn.class, "valid_records_" + tenantId);
    this.invalidRecords = Metrics.counter(ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn.class, "invalid_records_" + tenantId);
    this.latencyDistribution = Metrics.distribution(ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn.class, "ingest_latency_ms");
  }

  @ProcessElement
  public void processElement(@Element String json, OutputReceiver<TableRow> out, ProcessContext c) {
    long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
    try {
      JSONObject record = new JSONObject(json);
      if (isValid(record)) {
        out.output(new TableRow().set("data", record.toString()).set("tenant_id", c.sideInput(tenantId)));
        validRecords.inc();
      } else {
        invalidRecords.inc();
        emitBadRatioMetric(c);
      }
    } catch (Exception e) {
      invalidRecords.inc();
      emitBadRatioMetric(c);
    } finally {
      latencyDistribution.update(System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime);
    }
  }

  private void emitBadRatioMetric(ProcessContext c) {
    Metrics.gauge(ValidateAndEmitMetricsDoFn.class, "per_tenant_bad_ratio_" + c.sideInput(tenantId),
        () -> (double) invalidRecords.getCount() / (validRecords.getCount() + invalidRecords.getCount()) * 100);
  }
}
```

## Dashboard Recommendations
Group metrics by tenant using the **Group By** feature in Cloud Monitoring. Include panels for:
1. Ingest latency distribution (p50, p95, p99)
2. Bad ratio trend per tenant
3. Pipeline lag by tenant with threshold lines
4. Dead-letter bucket size as a data quality indicator

## Alert Configuration
- **Metric**: per_tenant_bad_ratio
- **Condition**: > 1% for 10 consecutive minutes
- **Notification**: Email/Slack/PagerDuty based on severity

